        "math_academy_id": "q-182088",
        "problem": "Find the value of $f(x)=x\u230a{e}^{x+1}\u230b$ at $x=0.75.$",
        "worked_solution": "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\u230ax\u230b$ equals the greatest integer that is less than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n\u230ax\u230b=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=0.75,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =0.75\u230a{e}^{0.75+1}\u230b \\\\  & =0.75\u230a{e}^{1.75}\u230b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u230a{e}^{1.75}\u230b=\u230a5.754\\,60\u2026\u230b=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0.75) & =0.75\u230a{e}^{1.75}\u230b \\\\  & =0.75(5) \\\\  & =3.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
        "deliberately_incorrect_submission": false,
